<BODY CLASS=myBodyTag>
<div class=mywhitetext>

<h3>Inner-Guild Dispute Procedures<o:p></o:p></h3>

<p>Primary rule: Praise in public, criticize in private <o:p></o:p></p>

<p>If two or more members within the guild have a conflict or disagreement,
they must resolve the dispute as follows: <o:p></o:p></p>

<ol start=1 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'>Take all disputes out of
     /guild chat. Arguments in guild chat will not be tolerated. It annoys
     people and damages morale. The two members that are in dispute <u>must</u>
     discuss the issue in private tells. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'>If the two individuals are
     unable to resolve the issue between them on their own, they may contact a
     Bone Guard member via private tells to help with the situation. The Bone
     Guard member will attempt to resolve the situation as quickly and as
     fairly as possible. If a Bone Guard member is not available, a higher
     ranking member (Blood Knight, Circle of Bones, Warlord) may be contacted,
     but in that order. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'>If either party is not
     satisfied with the decision, they can ask that a higher ranking member
     hear the complaint. At this point the Bone Guard should contact a superior
     ranking member and forward the situation to them. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'>If a Blood Knight or higher
     rank refuses to hear the dispute, the Bone Guard's decision stands. <o:p></o:p></li>
</ol>

<p class=MsoNormal>It should be STRONGLY noted that all attempts should be made
to resolve all disputes at the lowest rank possible. The higher ranking members
have many things to deal with and handling extra disputes not only makes their
lives more difficult, but it prevents them from focusing on their real duties.</p>

</div>

